for the past couple of months i've been  really enjoying my 16 inch m1 max  macbook pro for everything like snappy  web browsing on a daily basis the  incredible battery life that can last  days without needing a charge the  beautiful new mini led display for  watching shows and movies and of course  high performance for doing things like  photo editing in photoshop and video  editing in final cut pro but intel amd  and nvidia have been showing off new  processors and graphics chips at this  year's ces which will be going into new  laptops as soon as the end of this year  and from the looks of it apple's macbook  pro is gonna be seriously challenged on  every single front and even though the  m1 max is truly impressive for things  like video and photo editing programming  music production and more there are  still some areas where the m1 max just  isn't that great because of a lack of  proper software support take gaming for  example where the only optimized game  right out of the box is world of  warcraft which performs exceptionally  well when compared to a desktop rtx 3080  gpu but other than that the fps numbers  that we got in games that rely on  rosetta 2 translation and apps like  crossover 2.1 just weren't that  impressive and those are the games that  are actually supported since the latest  directx 12 api currently has zero  support with crossover and then if we  take a look at other things like raw  multi-threaded cpu performance and apps  like cinebench r23 amd's best 5900 hx  chip from last year is already right  there next to the 14 inch m1 max and  then going further looking at graphics  rendering performance the new blender  3.1 alpha build greatly improved  performance for many of the tests that  we ran  but the rtx 3080 within the razer blade  was still faster overall and it's even  worse for other rendering apps that  don't have decent support and to make  things worse intel amd and nvidia have  just unveiled some incredibly impressive  mobile chips that are gonna fly past  even the best version of the m1 max chip  so without further ado let's jump right  into some ces keynotes starting with  intel's our 12th gen h-series delivers  up to 40 percent higher performance than  our prior generation and there you go  they just unveiled the new 12th  generation mobile chips and these things  look promising look at that up to five  gigahertz clock speeds up to 14 cores  combining performance and efficiency  cores just like the m1 max is doing  these things are going to be very  powerful especially since they're saying  up to 40 percent higher performance gen  over gen and within their keynote intel  actually claimed that their new i9  processor is going to be faster than  apple's m1 max chip so check out this  chart right here you could see this is  basically a copy of what apple showed  off at their last event showing the m1  max having better performance per the  power that it uses better than the 5900  hx as you can see in that red line and  better than the last i9 11 980 hk and  you can see their new i-912 900 is above  and beyond what the m1 max can do which  is incredibly impressive and based on  this i fully believe when we actually  get them in our hands that those chips  are gonna have more raw performance than  the m1 max which is really disappointing  because with the m1 max chip it only got  better graphics performance instead of  better cpus now however the caveat is  that intel says that they'll use up to  115  watts of maximum power which is a ton  literally a ton of power as you can see  in this chart right here you can see  that a lot of these chips are using up  to 115  the i7s and the i9s the i5s actually go  up to 95 watts now keep in mind that  when we tested the m1 max ship the  maximum amount of power that it gave to  the cpu was 30 watts yes that's 30  instead of 115 so it kind of makes sense  why these alder like chips would be  faster and if you're wondering just how  much faster the new alder lakes are  going to be we already compared the m1  max 16 inch to the razer blade which had  the i9 11 900 h and in geekbench 5's  multi-core cpu test it scored up to 9300  points so the m1 max still had a good  lead but if you look over to how much  the top of the line 11 980 hk scored  that scored up to 10 000 points so if  you apply intel's 40 improvement we  should be getting around 14 000 which  will technically beat the m1 max and i'm  sure it'll do even better in cinebench  r23 so with that said i think there's a  pretty good chance that even some of  intel's i7 chips will be able to  outperform  the m1 max in terms of raw cpu  performance now that doesn't mean real  world performance and real task because  we are going to be testing that out as  soon as we get those new laptops so  definitely subscribe right now so you  don't miss out on those in-depth  comparisons but i guess we'll see and  finally intel did show off a new  technology which is very surprising  apparently they're going to be able to  integrate your iphone and your apple  watch with their new laptops and pcs so  you're essentially going to be able to  read your imessages through an intel  based pc which is very impressive and  one of the things that really  disappoints me about the new macbook pro  is that it does not support wi-fi 6e  which every single intel alder lake chip  is going to support so that's very  disappointing because i could have  bought a new wi-fi 6e router but i chose  wi-fi 6 instead because i just don't  have that on my macbook pro and the last  thing intel showed off was their new  deep link technology which basically  uses the integrated gpu within the alder  lake chip and the discrete intel arc  graphics chip together to improve  encoding speed by up to 1.4 times which  is actually very impressive so i guess  we'll see how that compares to the m1  max ship when we get our hands on those  and now let's move on to amd because  they also introduced some very  impressive laptop chips so let's listen  hey i'm proud to launch our amd ryzen  6000 series mobile 6000 series that  deliver leadership performance battery  life and much much more all right check  this out it's their zen 3 plus so it's  basically updated but the cool thing is  that it's on the new six nanometer  technology the new process node so it's  gonna be gaining in terms of efficiency  as well as performance with boost speeds  up to five gigahertz we're delivering an  average of 1.3 x faster performance  compared to the 5000 series now if you  didn't know how fast the amd chips were  check this out in terms of geekbench 5  the m1 max macbook pro was basically  killing the last top of the line 5900 hx  mobile chip that amd had so that's 12  600 compared to 9000 however if you  bring it into cinebench r23 you can see  right there that the 5900 hx is  literally right behind the m1 max in 100  cpu workloads now imagine adding 1.3  times to that number with the 6000  series yes it looks like it's gonna  destroy the m1 max chip and they might  even have some lower end models that are  going to be at the same level or even  outperform it so it's a little bit  disappointing that we don't have that  much cpu performance with the m1 max and  this right here is the real kicker amd  says that they're getting up to 24 hours  of battery life on a laptop now that's  probably using a laptop with a 99 watt  hour battery just like the 16 inch  macbook pro but it's because of the new  six nanometer process technology they  have the new power management they have  the new adaptive power control so  basically with all that said they say  they're getting up to that much now i'd  have to see it to believe it because we  tested the previous razer blade and it  had a horrible battery life so i guess  we'll have to test it out and see and  now getting to the next section they  have their new amd apus which is  basically a cpu with an integrated gpu  but here they're showing off their new  amd rd and a2 graphics architecture and  here you can see some pretty massive  gains in terms of fps compared to the  previous chips like the 1165 g7 which  goes into smaller 13-inch laptops look  at that 303 percent more fps and doom  eternal and a more popular title which  is cs go 146  so this basically shows that they're  gonna have actual competitive laptops  without dedicated graphics that you  could actually play games with and the  best part is that you have decent gaming  support with windows 11 instead of the  crappy situation with mac os where you  don't have that many games that are  supported and right here they're showing  off some new specs like for example they  got gen 4 pci express usb4 but as you  can see they have wi-fi 6e just like  intel and bluetooth low energy 5.2  compared to this macbook pro which just  has 5.0 which is also something that's  disappointing of course you have ddr5 on  those new chips and they also have hdmi  2.1 which the macbook pro does not have  unfortunately and apparently they also  have an av1 media engine which is also  nice for the windows side and finally  this slide is showing off that they're  gonna have these new chips into  notebooks or laptops starting february  so next month we're going to be getting  in these new laptops and comparing them  to this 16-inch macbook pro and now with  that said let's finally finish off with  nvidia's keynote and here they're  showing off a new rtx 3080 ti mobile  chip for laptops and this looks  absolutely insane basically the fastest  graphics in laptops ever and i fully  believe it's gonna outperform the m1 max  like crazy especially since they're  showing off up to 16 gigs of the fastest  gddr6 vram which is going to be very  impressive and what's blowing my mind is  that those laptops are going to start at  2500  which is exactly what this 16 inch  macbook pro starts at but that's without  the m1 max chip you actually have to pay  more especially if you want the fully  loaded you're paying 3 500  and then going further they showed off  the 3070 ti starting at only 1500 and  there's a chance that that chip is also  going to outperform the m1 max in terms  of graphics rendering and gaming and  other tasks like that which is crazy  like these guys are coming back with so  much performance at such a great value  it's just so impressive and one thing  that blew my mind was this chart in  terms of graphics rendering apps and  here they are showing off some massive  performance gains compared to a m1 max  macbook pro 16 inch like for example  blender cycles they're showing 10  compared to  153 in terms of minutes now obviously  that does not make sense and that's with  the blender cycles that does not support  the gpu that's actually cpu based and as  we know the new alpha build 3.1 of  blender finally supports it and it  definitely sped it up for us so you  shouldn't rely on this chart because  it's not showing the new alpha version  but i think what's the most accurate is  to look at redshift because redshift is  what apple used in their charts when  they showed off the m1 max ship so here  you can see 10 minutes instead of 28  that's almost three times faster and i  fully believe that this is realistic and  these chips are gonna be that much  faster than the macbook pro for graphics  rendering like that with that said i'm  very impressed with intel's nvidia's and  amd's ces keynotes because they're  showing off some very impressive gains  gains that i was not expecting at all so  this is very impressive and i'm excited  to get those in my hands so if you have  any thoughts on those keynotes or those  new chips definitely comment them down  below and if you're not already  subscribed do so right now because you  don't want to miss out on those laptop  comparisons compared to the m1 max so  thank you guys for watching check out  one of those two videos right there and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

